<title>CHILE: Chile's CCU prices ADRs at $16.</title>
<headline>Chile's CCU prices ADRs at $16.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean brewery Compania Cervecerias Unidas SA said it will sell its forthcoming issue of American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) at $16 per ADR.</p>
<p>The company has signed an underwriting agreement with a group led by Goldman Sachs &amp; Co to sell ADRs equivalent to 10,832,750 shares, said the statement to the Stocks and Values Superintendency.</p>
<p>This group also has an option to buy an additional 1,623,540 shares, it said.</p>
<p>CCU's ADRs were trading up 1.56 percent mid-afternoon Friday at 16-1/4.</p>
